{
  "borough": "Waltham Forest",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The application as submitted has failed to\r\nprovide drawings and supporting documentation consistent with the actual layout\r\nof the dwelling, noting that more bedrooms exist at ground floor level than\r\nillustrated on the drawings with less communal living/ dining spaces. As such,\r\nthe principle of development could not be established contrary to Policy 20 of\r\nthe adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&nbsp;",
    "The proposed development would result in a cramped and\r\nunsatisfactory form of living environment for existing and future occupiers\r\nfailing to meet minimum space standard requirements in relation to two of the\r\nsix bedrooms contrary to Policy 20, 53 and 56 of the adopted Waltham Forest\r\nLocal Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of consistent drawings and supporting documentation\r\nthe applicant has failed to demonstrate that the volume of occupiers would not\r\nover intensify the use. As such, the proposal would be contrary to Policy 57 of\r\nthe adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of consistent drawings and supporting documentation\r\nthe applicant has failed to demonstrate that the existing waste provision is\r\nsatisfactory for the level occupiers. As such, the proposal would be contrary\r\nto Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of consistent drawings and supporting documentation\r\nthe applicant has failed to demonstrate that the existing secure cycle storage\r\nis satisfactory for the level of occupiers. As such, the proposal would be\r\ncontrary to Policy 20, 61 &amp; Appendix 1 - Parking Standards of the adopted\r\nWaltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter into a legal&nbsp;agreement\r\n(S.106) and therefore would not in comply&nbsp;with Policy 94&nbsp;of the\r\nadopted Waltham Forest Local Plan Pt 1 (2024), in relation to the following\r\nplanning obligation&nbsp;requirements.\r\n\r\n\r\n Car\r\n     Free Development - the development is to be classified as car-free and\r\n     residents will not be eligible for parking permits.\r\n"
  ],
